# 11. CORE AI AND PLAGIARISM ENGINE ARCHITECTURE

The platform must be designed around two independent analysis services.

Do not hardcode the AI engines into frontend components.

Use modular APIs and service adapters.

## ENGINE 1 — PLAGIARISM DETECTION

Prepare an integration layer supporting:

- Text extraction.
- Text normalization.
- Sentence segmentation.
- N-gram comparison.
- Winnowing.
- MinHash.
- Semantic similarity.
- Embedding-based retrieval.
- Cross-encoder reranking.
- Source identification.
- Passage alignment.
- Citation detection.
- Institutional corpus comparison.

Potential technologies:
- Python.
- FastAPI.
- PostgreSQL.
- OpenSearch.
- Redis.
- Vector database.

The engine must return structured results containing:
- Similarity score.
- Matched passages.
- Source references.
- Source metadata.
- Match type.
- Text offsets.
- Confidence or matching evidence.

Do not present inaccessible web pages as verified sources.

## ENGINE 2 — AI-GENERATED CONTENT DETECTION

Prepare an independent multilingual detection service.

Architecture should support:
- XLM-RoBERTa.
- Transformer-based classification.
- Token-level classification.
- Linguistic feature extraction.
- Stylometric features.
- Ensemble classification.
- Probability calibration.
- Language-specific evaluation.
- Human-written versus AI-generated training data.

The service must return:
- Document-level indicator.
- Passage-level indicators.
- Confidence information where validated.
- Analysis coverage.
- Model version.
- Language.
- Inconclusive segments.
- Technical explanations.

Do not pretend that a trained model exists if it has not been connected.

## ENGINE ADAPTER PATTERN

Implement independent interfaces:

PlagiarismEngineAdapter:
- analyze(document)
- getStatus()
- getVersion()

AIDetectionEngineAdapter:
- analyze(document)
- getStatus()
- getVersion()

Support:
- Demo implementation.
- External API implementation.
- Future proprietary model implementation.

Make it possible to replace either engine without rebuilding the frontend.

